    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for June 28th is anchored by a high-upside outfield configuration, with **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) serving as our strongest plays. Both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Littell, combining a high base projection with an outstanding 19% SP skill boost and a +16% park factor. Similarly, **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) is an elite UTIL option today; his 0.374 xwOBA profile and a +12% dynamic platoon advantage against Me. Kelly make him a standout, while **Daulton Varsho** (66.20) rounds out the top tier\u2014his score is bolstered by a 91% SB-friendly delivery from the opposing pitcher, providing the exact type of category-scarcity upside we prioritize.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Luis Arraez**, whose 41.85 score keeps him on the bubble but ultimately below our efficiency threshold for today. While he offers stability, the volatility of facing an elite arm like Sale\u2014which dragged his SP skill projection down by 19%\u2014made him a sub-optimal start compared to the volume of higher-ceiling platoon plays like **Tyler Freeman** (63.25) and **Lawrence Butler** (60.97). We are taking a calculated risk with **Matt Chapman** (42.80) at 3B; despite the daunting challenge of facing Sale, his leadoff spot and the \"Wind Out\" benefit marginally keep him above the bench floor. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risk profile of our infield. **Geraldo Perdomo** (44.81), **Bryson Stott** (46.26), and **Gavin Sheets** (46.43) are all positioned in the \"Marginal\" range. **Gavin Sheets** gets a necessary boost from favorable wind conditions and a platoon edge against Sheehan, but the SP skill discount is heavy across the board for our middle infielders. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** still sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on the high-efficiency scoring of our outfield to carry the load today. Keep a close eye on the late-afternoon weather reports, as any shifts in wind direction could further suppress the ceilings of our lower-scored starters.",
